        "title": "Inflammation and Tissue Repair",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**It explicitly defers** the *immune-cell biology and signaling* — how neutrophils,\nmacrophages, and lymphocytes develop and what their receptors do at molecular depth — to\n`immunology/`; the *organism biology* of any infectious trigger to `microbiology/`/\n`virology/`; the *disease entities* (specific inflammatory or fibrotic diseases) to\n`disease/`; and *normal physiology* to `human-biology/`. Inflammation is owned here as a\n**tissue-level mechanism**, not as immunology and not as a disease list."
    },
