      "text": "## The Big Picture: Inflammation Is a Defense Program With a Repair Back-End"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-INFLAMMATION-AND-TISSUE-REPAIR.md#007",
      "path": [
        "02-INFLAMMATION-AND-TISSUE-REPAIR.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:pathology:02-inflammation-and-tissue-repair]",
        "canonical_path": "pathology/02-INFLAMMATION-AND-TISSUE-REPAIR.md",
        "concepts": "[acute-inflammation, chemical-mediators, chronic-inflammation, granuloma, tissue-repair, wound-healing-fibrosis]",
        "current_path": "pathology/02-INFLAMMATION-AND-TISSUE-REPAIR.md",
        "id": "maxim:pathology:inflammation-and-tissue-repair",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "pathology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inflammation]",
        "section": "pathology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inflammation and Tissue Repair",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The novice mental model is \"inflammation = swelling, and swelling is bad.\" The expert model is\na **protective response program** with a defined lifecycle: **detect** an injurious agent or\ndead tissue, **recruit** plasma proteins and leukocytes to the site, **destroy or contain**\nthe agent, and then **resolve** and **repair**. Inflammation is fundamentally *beneficial* —\nwithout it, infections go unchecked and wounds never heal — but it is a **double-edged**\nprogram: the same machinery that clears a pathogen damages bystander tissue, and if it fails\nto switch off, it becomes the engine of chronic disease and scarring."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-INFLAMMATION-AND-TISSUE-REPAIR.md#008",
      "path": [
        "02-INFLAMMATION-AND-TISSUE-REPAIR.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:pathology:02-inflammation-and-tissue-repair]",
        "canonical_path": "pathology/02-INFLAMMATION-AND-TISSUE-REPAIR.md",
        "concepts": "[acute-inflammation, chemical-mediators, chronic-inflammation, granuloma, tissue-repair, wound-healing-fibrosis]",
        "current_path": "pathology/02-INFLAMMATION-AND-TISSUE-REPAIR.md",
        "id": "maxim:pathology:inflammation-and-tissue-repair",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "pathology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inflammation]",
        "section": "pathology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inflammation and Tissue Repair",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHE INFLAMMATION -> REPAIR LIFECYCLE  (this guide owns the whole arc)\n====================================================================\n  injury / infection / necrotic cells (from 01)\n        |\n        v\n  ===== ACUTE INFLAMMATION (minutes-days; neutrophil-led) =====\n  [ RECOGNIZE ]  danger signals + pattern receptors fire\n  [ VASCULAR  ]  vasodilation -> increased permeability -> exudate\n  [ CELLULAR  ]  leukocytes marginate -> adhere -> transmigrate ->\n                 chemotax -> phagocytose\n        |\n        v\n  ===== OUTCOME FORK =====\n   RESOLUTION        ABSCESS          CHRONIC           SCAR / FIBROSIS\n   (best case:       (walled-off      INFLAMMATION      (repair overshoots ->\n    clear + repair)   pus)            (persistent)       matrix replaces tissue)\n        |                                 |                    |\n        v                                 v                    v\n  ===== REPAIR ARM =====\n  REGENERATION  (functional tissue restored — if the scaffold survives and\n                 the cells can divide)   vs   SCAR (collagen fills the gap)\n```"
    },
